# A landscape's own kind (mechanics pass 3a; BiomeDef.roster `over`): the hauler
# down in the limestone caves works the dark by ear. Held under the target key,
# the slate reads it off the same row it fights by: sees 3, hears 13, a slower
# pace, and a 780 ms tell where the bonelands' hauler tells in 600. By day in
# the dark of a cave it carries its own light (MachineModel.land_dark).
#   tools/tour.sh tours/cave_hauler.tour --seed=7 --realm=underground --hour=11
coast calm
# Out onto the open floor first: at the shaft foot the spawner stands it behind
# the pipe run, and a frame of the pipe is not a frame of the machine.
walk -1,0 1.6
wait 0.6
spawn hauler
wait 0.6
shot 01-the-cave-hauler-by-its-own-light with mob:hauler
hold target
await target 5
wait 0.6
shot 02-the-cave-hauler-read-by-its-own-row with mob:hauler,target
release target
# Its tell in the dark: the working part warming as it winds up. A worker bites
# only once it is struck, so it is struck first.
try 4
walkto part 3
tap swing
await hit 1.5
end
await tell 10
wait 0.35
shot 03-its-tell-in-the-dark with mob:hauler
